$a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-3a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-4b-3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-4b=-3a-4b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3.\n$$"}]}
